# Optional persistent ordinary CTF history capture — Source proposal 01

This is a held Source-only proposal. It has not been installed, formatted, built,
run, compared, or used to change a gate. Canonical Rust/docs and Native inputs,
policies, captures, binaries and results are untouched.

## Scope and actual ownership

The existing ordinary initializer produces the real public coefficients and
persistent `CtfSurfaceLifecycle`. The existing ordinary timestep calls its begin
and commit once at the existing locations. This proposal adds passive borrowed
observations around those real operations; it does not replay Native prestate,
initialize a second owner, compute coefficients, change solver operands, or add
another simulation pipeline. Base's SUR04 arithmetic proposal is disjoint.

Runtime changes are one new public capture module, its declaration, and additive
hooks in `ctf_surface_lifecycle.rs`. The ep_run example owns JSON/streaming and
uses the existing `run_arbitrary_idf` once with ordinary compatibility settings.
No dependency is added. Runtime has no JSON adapter and no growing event ledger.

## Exact boundaries

| Rust event | Actual seam | Clock facts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| BeginEntry | Before begin-wrapper checks/stores | passed caller clock; independent actual timestep argument |
| InitializationInput | After existing report reset, before selected Init | passed clock; current owner clock still absent |
| InitializationReturned | After selected Init, before initialized/current/lagged stores | same passed clock; no accepted-current inference |
| BeginReturned / BeginFailed | After real wrapper Result and sticky-error store | caller/current/last remain separate |
| HistoryUpdateInput | After actual current temperature synchronization, before selected update | accepted current clock passed directly |
| HistoryUpdateReturned | After actual selected update, before lagged copies | actual returned SimpleShift or MasterHistories route |
| HistoryCommitBeforeClockRelease | After lagged copies and last-committed store | current clock still owned; last committed already updated |
| CommitReturned / CommitFailed | After real wrapper Result and sticky-error store | saved actual commit clock; successful return has current absent |

The independent begin timestep argument is present only at BeginEntry and its
wrapper return/failure. Selected-function and commit events have null in that
field; their actual caller clock retains its own hours/seconds. A missing clock,
public owner, stale generation, consumer mismatch or failed history operation
remains the real typed failure. A missing lifecycle emits no fabricated visit.

## Stream contract and field map

The example takes four positional arguments: input, weather, fresh run output
directory, and a fresh NDJSON path. It preserves default ordinary calculation and
output behavior; trace is Off, no hour override, no oracle/Native invocation.
The stream file is create-new. Each record is one JSON line without a sample cap.
Schemas are `ctf10-persistent-ordinary-history-stream.v1` (header/summary),
`ctf10-persistent-ordinary-generation.v1`, and
`ctf10-persistent-ordinary-history-event.v1`.

Every event has boundary, rust_local_generation_id, caller_clock,
begin_timestep_seconds_argument, outdoor_dry_bulb_c, owner, public,
model_catalog, consumer_surfaces, selected_inputs, selected_context,
update_route, error, and counted_as_PASS:false. Owner retains initialized,
current_clock, last_committed_clock, first failure, full history, actual HT/opaque
groups and separate AllHT order. Selected inputs/context are borrowed only at
the real selected-function boundaries, never reconstructed at later events.

History includes actual surface layout and all four normal arrays, every19 row
and every column; optional masters with all four arrays and counter; optional
five scratch arrays; update_first_time; and four report arrays. Rust allocation
presence and full vector lengths are explicit. Native Objexx lower/upper bounds
are unavailable here and are never invented. Temperature units are C, history
and scratch flux W/m2, conduction reports W, flux reports W/m2, SumTime hours.
Every f64 uses the existing literal scalar class/16-hex-bit serializer.

Public rows retain construction/order/material associations, all12 fixed19
arrays/counts/dt/U, aggregate, final flags and typed unavailable/stop facts.
Model catalog retains all Zone/Space/surface/construction rows in actual input
order and raw Rust IDs/names/layers/vertices/boundaries. Consumer rows retain
current/lagged CTF storage, exact active coefficient views, constants, current
surface/reference/convection inputs, actual five inside gain slots and stored
heat_gain_to_zone_w. This is boundary custody, not a per-iteration SUR04 trace.

The generation key remains a borrowed exact typed runtime owner. The example
assigns a Rust-local ID only by actual key Eq, cloning once per distinct key in
the observer. It emits genuine producer context and complete compiled source
witnesses once per generation. It does not expose a guessed digest or assert
Native key/ID equality. Clocks retain actual phase Warmup{day}/Run{day}, record
index, begin flags, day/hour/substep, SimTimeSteps and hours/seconds bits.
Native environment ID/name, KickOff and calendar fields are explicitly absent.

## Optional sink and failure behavior

Disabled capture returns before boxing a sink and constructs no observation,
owner clone, JSON tree or event collection in the solver. Active callbacks borrow
immutable owners synchronously. The callback must be passive/non-reentrant.
Nested and unwinding guards restore the previous sink. A callback panic follows
normal Rust unwind semantics; this is not claimed as a recoverable solver error.

The example retains its first stream I/O error and counts later callbacks without
writing/serializing more records. It never substitutes a solver Result. After
the actual ordinary caller returns, observer failure returns a failing observer
exit and preserves the partial file. Summary capture_complete describes I/O
completion only; boundary reachability and numerical comparison remain false.
Zero events, absent owners, missing footer, failed/unreturned calls and unmatched
branches cannot establish coverage or PASS.

## Proposed verification and future admission

Four unexecuted tests use the genuine existing ordinary input fixture and actual
initializer: captured vs uncaptured two distinct successful clocks/owners; real
MissingCallerClock retention without commit; disabled sink and20002 uncapped
failure events; nested/unwinding restoration. The fixture prefix, scalar helper
and public-storage helper are literal accepted Source reuse with checked ranges.

Root must review/install the exact mapping, inspect actual formatter deltas, run
quality, capture full Cargo SourceSnapshot/artifact provenance and guard actual
input/weather identities before any run. No future receipts or hashes are bound
here. Pairing policy must be settled before outputs: exact named/associated
surface identities and actual phase/day/hour/substep; duplicate shared keys are
ambiguous failures, never ordinal/occurrence joins or normalized warmup phases.
Native stage/scope/parent-return custody stays independent. Selected direct
history parity does not certify this future persistent ordinary handoff.
